course: dictionary
lesson: 16099
title: Weaning and changing habits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Weaning means slowly moving from one thing to another. A baby animal is weaned when it stops drinking only its mother's milk and starts eating other food. «The lambs are being weaned onto grass now.» The word "slowly" is the clue: the change happens bit by bit, not all at once.
explain: The word also works for habits. «Dad is weaning me off screens, so I use them a little less each day.» Weaning off means cutting down slowly, step by step. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "Dad is slowly cutting down my screens" still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Weaning means slowly getting used to something new, such as solid food instead of milk.
fact: «Weaning off» means slowly giving up something you depend on or are used to.
fact: Other phrases to remember: wean off, wean onto, be weaned from.
fact: Parents often start weaning a baby onto mashed food at around six months old.
fact: In Scotland, a «wean» is a child. This is a different Scots word, not the same as weaning.
exercise: «The lambs are being weaned onto grass now.» What does weaning mean here? | Counting the sheep | Running fast in the field | *Slowly changing from milk to other food | Sleeping all day
exercise: «Dad is weaning me off screens, so I use them a little less each day.» What does weaning off mean? | Turning the screen up loud | Buying a new screen | *Slowly cutting down | Stopping straight away, all at once
exercise: In Scotland, what does «wean» mean? | A young animal | *A child | Lots of rain | A kind of bread
test: «Mum began weaning the baby onto mashed banana.» What does weaning mean? | Taking the baby out for a walk | *Slowly introducing solid food alongside milk | Stopping all food forever at once | Feeding the baby sweets
test: Which phrase means slowly giving up a habit? | Warm up | Wash out | Wake up | *Wean off
exam: Which sentence uses weaning correctly? | The boat is weaning across the bay | The bus is weaning at the stop | The cat is weaning in the sun | *The calf is weaning onto grass now
